From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: siphasher is not only for tests

adblock-rust parses procedural filters with selectors and cssparser,
whose phf tables hash with siphasher, so the crate is no longer
test-only, as patch 0287 has it for regex. The crates that need it come
from packages/domicile-engine/crates/CRATES.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`. Guarded by guard-ad-blocking.
---
 third_party/rust/siphasher/v1/BUILD.gn | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/rust/siphasher/v1/BUILD.gn b/third_party/rust/siphasher/v1/BUILD.gn
index e1c69dcd1f..652ea2aa92 100644
--- a/third_party/rust/siphasher/v1/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/rust/siphasher/v1/BUILD.gn
@@ -38,7 +38,10 @@ cargo_crate("lib") {
   # //third_party/rust/chromium_crates_io/Cargo.toml to use
   # it from first-party code.
   visibility = [ "//third_party/rust/*" ]
-  testonly = true
+
+  # Domicile's engine fork: phf_shared, which adblock-rust's CSS parsing
+  # (selectors, cssparser) builds on, hashes with it, so it is not only for
+  # tests. See packages/domicile-engine/crates/CRATES.
 
   #####################################################################
   # Tweaking which GN `config`s apply to this target.
-- 
2.43.0

